# Line endings are normalised for a cross-platform plugin: Git stores LF, and every platform's
# checkout gets LF. Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites every source
# file to CRLF, so CRLF leaks into a Linux/macOS contributor's tree and into the published npm
# tarball — and the vendored .py / .mjs sources then differ byte-for-byte between platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only artefacts keep CRLF so cmd.exe parses them. Nothing ships one today; the rule
# is here so a future launcher wrapper does not arrive LF-only and fail on Windows.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
